<title>USA: Pittsburgh Home to buy back stock.</title>
<headline>Pittsburgh Home to buy back stock.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pittsburgh Home Financial Corp, the holding company for Pittsburgh Home Savings Bank, said on Tuesday its board of directors authorized the repurchase of up to 109,106 shares or about five percent of the company's outstanding stock.  </p>
<p>The company said it was authorized to make repurchases from time to time in open-market transactions depending on market conditions.</p>
<p>Repurchased shares would be held as treasury stock and would be available for general corporate purposes, company said.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
